<library>
<description>Fiducial marker for pick-and-place optical alignment.

Written here because Fusion's managed libraries have no fiducial - `holes.lbr` covers
mounting holes only. JLCPCB list fiducials as Necessary for Standard PCBA.

To JLCPCB's usual spec:
  - 1.00 mm bare copper pad, top layer
  - 2.00 mm solder-mask opening (so 0.5 mm of clear mask all round)
  - NO solder paste - the pad must stay bare, so cream is disabled
  - 3.00 mm copper keep-out, to stop a ground pour reaching the mark

Placement rules, which matter more than the pad does:
  - THREE per board, near the corners
  - placed ASYMMETRICALLY, so the camera cannot read the orientation two ways.
    Three in a symmetric arrangement is worse than useless - it lets the machine
    align a mirrored or rotated board with confidence.
  - at least 5 mm in from the board edge
  - nothing else within the 3 mm keep-out, and no silkscreen across them

The symbol carries no pins, so these never appear in a net and never trip ERC. They
DO appear as parts, so exclude FID1..FID3 when generating the BOM and CPL - the same
way DIGIT1-4 are excluded. There is nothing for a machine to place here; the fiducial
IS the board.

If JLCPCB panelise the order they normally add their own fiducials to the rails.
Ours align this board rather than the panel, which is the more useful of the two.</description>
<packages>
<package name="FIDUCIAL_1MM">
<description>1 mm copper, 2 mm mask opening, 3 mm keep-out, no paste</description>
<smd name="1" x="0" y="0" dx="1" dy="1" layer="1" roundness="100" stop="no" cream="no"/>
<circle x="0" y="0" radius="1" width="0" layer="29"/>
<circle x="0" y="0" radius="1.5" width="0" layer="41"/>
<circle x="0" y="0" radius="1.5" width="0.05" layer="39"/>
<circle x="0" y="0" radius="1.5" width="0.05" layer="51"/>
<text x="-1.5" y="1.9" size="1" layer="25">&gt;NAME</text>
</package>
</packages>
<symbols>
<symbol name="FIDUCIAL">
<circle x="0" y="0" radius="1.016" width="0.254" layer="94"/>
<circle x="0" y="0" radius="0.508" width="1.016" layer="94"/>
<text x="-2.54" y="2.286" size="1.778" layer="95">&gt;NAME</text>
<text x="-2.54" y="-4.064" size="1.778" layer="96">&gt;VALUE</text>
</symbol>
</symbols>
<devicesets>
<deviceset name="FIDUCIAL" prefix="FID">
<description>Pick-and-place fiducial. 1 mm copper, 2 mm mask opening, no paste.
&lt;b&gt;Three per board, asymmetrically placed.&lt;/b&gt; No pins - never appears in a net.
Exclude from the BOM and CPL.</description>
<gates>
<gate name="G$1" symbol="FIDUCIAL" x="0" y="0"/>
</gates>
<devices>
<device name="" package="FIDUCIAL_1MM">
<technologies>
<technology name="">
<attribute name="BOM" value="EXCLUDE" constant="no"/>
<attribute name="VALUE" value="FIDUCIAL" constant="no"/>
</technology>
</technologies>
</device>
</devices>
</deviceset>
</devicesets>
</library>
</drawing>
</eagle>
